# REVERSED: Proto-Iranian -> Proto-Indo-Iranian
# Source: team addition (tree/additions.yaml); no Index Diachronica section exists.
#   Drafted by Claude from:
#   [Skjærvø 2009] Skjærvø, P. O. (2009), "Old Iranian", in Windfuhr, G. (ed.),
#     The Iranian Languages, London: Routledge, section "From Proto-Indo-Iranian to
#     Proto-Iranian" (title approximate; § ? / p. ? for the team to fill in).
#   Each rule carries its own citation (team decision 2026-11-27).
# STATUS: DRAFT by Claude, awaiting team review.
#
# Input: Proto-Iranian in IPA as produced by Old-Persian.lsc (puθra, d͡zast, xʃaθr, hwat).
# Output: Proto-Indo-Iranian in the notation of the Sanskrit chain's Proto-Indo-Aryan.lsc,
#   so Persian and Sanskrit candidates meet in one notation:
#   tʃ dʒ = palatovelar reflexes (Wiktionary *ć *ȷ́); c ɟ = palatalized velars (*č *ǰ);
#   voiceless aspirates = stop + h₂.
#
# Forward changes, Proto-Indo-Iranian > Proto-Iranian:
#   S1  *s > *h before vowels and sonorants (*sapta > *hafta 'seven', *swapnas > *hwapnah
#       'sleep')                                                   [Skjærvø 2009, p. ?]
#   S2  voiced aspirates lose aspiration (*bʰrātar > *brātar 'brother')
#                                                                  [Skjærvø 2009, p. ?]
#   S3  *p *t *k > *f *θ *x before consonants (*sapta > *hafta; *putra > *puθra 'son')
#                                                                  [Skjærvø 2009, p. ?]
#   S4  voiceless aspirates *pʰ *tʰ *kʰ > *f *θ *x (*pantʰās > *panθāh 'path')
#                                                                  [Skjærvø 2009, p. ?]
#   S5  palatovelar reflexes *ć *ȷ́ > *c *j [t͡s d͡z]; *č *ǰ unchanged [t͡ʃ d͡ʒ]
#                                                                  [Skjærvø 2009, p. ?]
#
# HOW THIS FILE WORKS
# One simultaneous block (first match wins); no mergers. Contexts decide S3 versus S4.
#
# REVIEW NOTES
# - S1 is reversed everywhere: Proto-Iranian h has no other source.
# - S2 is not reversed. b d ɡ stay plain rather than branching to bʱ dʱ ɡʱ: the Step 6
#   cost of a missing aspiration is only 0.25, and branching every voiced stop would
#   multiply the candidates (team decision pending; noted 2026-11-27).
# - S3/S4: f θ x before a consonant reverse to p t k; elsewhere to p h₂, t h₂, k h₂.
# - Laryngeals (H) are not restored: Proto-Iranian kept no consonantal trace of them.
#   Sanskrit candidates with H pay one insertion (1.8125) against Persian ones.
# - q (from the modern-Persian ɣ/q branch) has no Proto-Indo-Iranian source and maps to k.

Symbol aː, iː, uː, r̩, t͡s, d͡z, t͡ʃ, d͡ʒ, tʃ, dʒ, h₂, xʷ

Class cons {p, b, t, d, k, ɡ, q, f, θ, x, xʷ, s, z, ʃ, ʒ, h, m, n, r, l, w, j, t͡s, d͡z, t͡ʃ, d͡ʒ, r̩}

proto-iranian-to-pii:
    # S3 reversed: f θ x before a consonant < p t k   [Skjærvø 2009, p. ?]
    f => p / _ @cons
    θ => t / _ @cons
    x => k / _ @cons
    # S4 reversed: f θ x elsewhere < voiceless aspirates (stop + h₂)   [Skjærvø 2009, p. ?]
    f => p h₂
    θ => t h₂
    x => k h₂
    xʷ => k h₂ w
    # S1 reversed: h < s   [Skjærvø 2009, p. ?]
    h => s
    # S5 reversed: c j < ć ȷ́; č ǰ < č ǰ (Sanskrit-chain notation)   [Skjærvø 2009, p. ?]
    t͡s => tʃ
    d͡z => dʒ
    t͡ʃ => c
    d͡ʒ => ɟ
    # Team note: q has no Proto-Indo-Iranian source
    q => k
